Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.00,0:00:11.62,Default,,0,0,0,,On a hill above Kurukshetra,\Na head keeps watch.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.02,0:00:15.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Not a ghost.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.10,0:00:18.97,Default,,0,0,0,,A promise.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.47,0:00:24.34,Default,,0,0,0,,His name was Barbarika.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.34,0:00:27.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandson of Bhima.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.01,0:00:33.33,Default,,0,0,0,,He carried three arrows,\Nand a vow to side with the weaker army.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.33,0:00:38.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Krishna tested him with a smile.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.84,0:00:42.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you pin every leaf\Nof this peepal tree?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.82,0:00:46.50,Default,,0,0,0,,One arrow rose.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.10,0:00:52.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Leaves fell like rain,\Nexcept the ones Krishna crushed under his foot.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.32,0:00:58.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Barbarika's second arrow\Nhunted even those.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.83,0:01:03.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Krishna saw the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.20,0:01:08.44,Default,,0,0,0,,This boy could empty\Nboth armies before dusk.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.64,0:01:13.73,Default,,0,0,0,,So Krishna asked for a gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.23,0:01:17.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Not his bow.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.40,0:01:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,His head.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.77,0:01:29.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Barbarika knelt, and gave it,\Nso he could see the war he was never allowed to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.79,0:01:35.89,Default,,0,0,0,,From the hill, he watched\Nbrothers kill brothers.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.09,0:01:43.48,Default,,0,0,0,,And when the dust settled, he whispered\Nwhat only the dead may know.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.48,0:01:47.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Victory has many hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.98,0:01:50.85,Default,,0,0,0,,But dharma has a cost.
